            <section class="info-section" id="access">
                <h2>Signing in</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Passwords are hashed with bcrypt and never stored or logged in readable form.</li>
                    <li>Sign-in attempts are rate limited, and repeated incorrect passwords lock the profile for a short time.</li>
                    <li>Sign-in errors don’t say whether it was the email or the password that was wrong.</li>
                    <li>Optional two-step verification uses a six-digit code from any authenticator app. Each code works once.</li>
                    <li>Sessions use HTTP-only cookies, the session identifier is replaced at sign-in, and sessions end after 30 minutes without activity or 24 hours at most.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="controls">
                <h2>Controls in your hands</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Security center</strong> — review recent sign-ins and devices, end any other session, and see a timeline of security events.</li>
                    <li><strong>Card controls</strong> — freeze a card instantly, switch off online, contactless, ATM or international use, and set spending limits. One action freezes every card at once.</li>
                    <li><strong>Recovery codes</strong> — eight single-use backup codes reset your password without email. Using one signs out every other session.</li>
                    <li><strong>Privacy mode</strong> — hide balances on screen when you’re in public.</li>
                    <li><strong>Your data</strong> — download a JSON copy of your profile and activity.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="app">
                <h2>Inside the application</h2>
                <p>Every form and request that changes something carries an anti-forgery token. The server checks that each account, card or payee belongs to you before acting. Money movements update both sides of the ledger in a single database transaction, so a transfer can never half-happen. Account and administrative actions are written to an audit log. Pages are sent with a content security policy and other protective headers.</p>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="limits">
                <h2>Limits worth knowing</h2>
                <p>No independent security review, penetration test or certification has been performed. These features demonstrate good practice; they are not a guarantee. Secure cookies and encrypted connections depend on the app being hosted over HTTPS. Willow should never hold real personal or financial information.</p>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="habits">
                <h2>Good habits</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Use a unique password and turn on two-step verification.</li>
                    <li>Store recovery codes somewhere private and offline.</li>
                    <li>Sign out on shared devices and end sessions you don’t recognise.</li>
                    <li>Remember: Willow will never ask for your password, codes or card details by message.</li>
                </ul>
                <p><a class="text-link" href="/insights/everyday-security-habits">Read the full guide to everyday security habits</a>.</p>
            </section>
